<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tenterfield Oration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tenterfield Oration was a speech given on 24 October 1889 at the School of Arts in Tenterfield, New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a>, by the colony's premier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-parkes">Sir Henry Parkes</a>. Citing a report on colonial defence, he called for the federation of the Australian colonies under one government and parliament. The speech led to the Federation Conference of 1890 and the conventions that drafted the constitution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tenterfield-oration.jpg" alt="Tenterfield Oration" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dewhurst, A. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StateLibQld_1_236927_View_of_Tenterfield,_New_South_Wales,_1887.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
